  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/beneficial-ownership
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter distinguishes beneficial ownership from legal ownership when examining
      capital.
    evidence:
    - page: page/84/0008
      quote: "84071 Only the capital which people are the beneficial owners of is included when working
        out what\ncapital they have.\n\n\n84072 People are beneficial owners of capital if they have a
        beneficial interest in it. A person is the joint\nbeneficial owner of capital if more than one
        person has a beneficial interest in the same capital.\n\n\n84073 A person whose name the capital
        is in is called the legal owner. A person is the joint legal owner of\ncapital if more than one
        person is the legal owner of the same capital."
      locator: DMG 84071–84073
